From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad Nicholas <70774+bradn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 01:50:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Move iOS settings to the Settings app; load remote images
 on iOS

Settings: appearance, themes, text size and line width move from a
toolbar popover to Settings > Apps > Downright (Settings.bundle). The
store keeps one UserDefaults key per setting, migrates the JSON blob
earlier builds saved (at launch, so the Settings page is right before a
document opens), and re-applies on returning from the Settings app.

Remote images: MarkdownRender gains a RemoteImageLoading hook on the
fragment context; https: images (own-line Markdown images and HTML
<img>) render only when a host installs a loader. The Mac app and Quick
Look never do, so they stay blocked or inert. The iOS app's loader is
cookie-free and size- and time-limited, draws SVG through a hidden,
script-free WebKit canvas, and is controlled by a Load Remote Images
switch (on by default).

SafeHTML now drops harmless presentational attributes (width, class,
style, ...) and accepts unquoted values instead of rejecting the block,
and marks https: images as .remoteImage. Images inside a paragraph or
link still are not drawn as pictures; that needs inline image layout.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
